 its timely implementation.\\n3. Future work on increasing the scientific potential of the department:\\n\\u2022 creating sufficient conditions for conducting scientific research work of young staff of the department.\\n\\u2022 To select students from among the graduates of the department\'s and master\'s programs with high knowledge and social culture, to improve their language proficiency and to interest them in scientific work;\\n\\u2022 Interest among gifted students, masters and teachers to develop startup ideas, innovative practical and fundamental projects and win grands.\\n4. Future work on improving the foreign relations of the department:\\n\\u2022 Find the universities of higher education in the foreign TOP 1000, having the trends and specialties of study in the department;\\n\\u2022 sign a memorandum of cooperation with higher educational institutions, establish scientific ties with professors and teachers, jointly implement foreign grants and publish scientific articles included in the SCOPUS database;\\n\\u2022 Organization of internships of the leading professors of the department in the top 1000 foreign universities and attract foreign university professors to the department and establish academic exchange.\"]}]', 'Кафедра сельскохозяйственных и водохозяйственных инженерных технологий', 'The basis of the department \"Agricultural and water management technique technology\" was established as a higher educational institution in the education system of the Republic of Uzbekistan on August 20, 2010 under the name of the department \"Genera', '2026-07-26 00:16:43', '2026-07-27 06:31:48');
INSERT INTO `department_translations` (`id`, `department_id`, `locale`, `name`, `short_name`, `description`, `content_sections`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('36', '9', 'ar', 'قسم التقنيات الهندسية الزراعية وإدارة المياه', 'قسم التقنيات الهندسية الزراعية وإدارة المياه', 'The basis of the department \"Agricultural and water management technique technology\" was established as a higher educational institution in the education system of the Republic of Uzbekistan on August 20, 2010 under the name of the department \"General professional sciences, mechanization of water economy and melioration works\", then due to the insufficient number of quotas of the branch, it was named under the department \"Hydromelioration\" The first department was appointed Acting Head of the department, Ph.D., associate professor Hasanov I.S. Lessons are conducted in the following subjects, relevant to the department.\nDue to the lack of specialized teachers in the newly created department, professors and teachers from the former Tashkent Institute of Irrigation and Melioration (TIMI) and Bukhara Institute of Food and Light Industry Technologies (Bux OO and Yesti) came to the department and provided methodological consultations to the teachers of the department.\nIn 2010-2011 academic year there were 7 professors and 2 technical staff at the department, including 5 candidates of science, associate professors and 2 assistant teachers, whose scientific potential was 71%. Professor-teachers who worked at the department during that period are listed below.', '[{\"key\":\"overview\",\"title\":\"\\u0646\\u0638\\u0631\\u0629 \\u0639\\u0627\\u0645\\u0629\",\"items\":[\"Department of Agricultural and Water Management Engineering Technologies     \\n\\nHead of the Department of Agriculture and Water Resources\\nRajabov Yarash Jabborovich\\n Reception time: Dushanba-Juma (14:00-16:00 gacha)\\n Phone: +998 (93) 138 84 20\\n Email: -\"]},{\"key\":\"history\",\"title\":\"\\u062a\\u0627\\u0631\\u064a\\u062e \\u0627\\u0644\\u0642\\u0633\\u0645\",\"items\":[\"The basis of the department \\\"Agricultural and water management technique technology\\\" was established as a higher educational institution in the education system of the Republic of Uzbekistan on August 20, 2010 under the name of the department \\\"General professional sciences, mechanization of water economy and melioration works\\\", then due to the insufficient number of quotas of the branch, it was named under the department \\\"Hydromelioration\\\" The first department was appointed Acting Head of the department, Ph.D., associate professor Hasanov I.S. Lessons are conducted in the following subjects, relevant to the department.\\nDue to the lack of specialized teachers in the newly created department, professors and teachers from the former Tashkent Institute of Irrigation and Melioration (TIMI) and Bukhara Institute of Food and Light Industry Technologies (Bux OO and Yesti) came to the department and provided methodological consultations to the teachers of the department.\\nIn 2010-2011 academic year there were 7 professors and 2 technical staff at the department, including 5 candidates of science, associate professors and 2 assistant teachers, whose scientific potential was 71%. Professor-teachers who worked at the department during that period are listed below.\"]},{\"key\":\"staff\",\"title\":\"\\u0623\\u0639\\u0636\\u0627\\u0621 \\u0647\\u064a\\u0626\\u0629 \\u0627\\u0644\\u062a\\u062f\\u0631\\u064a\\u0633 \\u0641\\u064a \\u0627\\u0644\\u0642\\u0633\\u0645\",\"items\":[\"Doctor of philosophy in technical sciences, associate professor\\nRadjabov Yarash Jabborovich\",\"Candidate of Technical Sciences, Associate Professor\\nHasanov Ibrahim Subhonovich\",\"Doctor of Technical Sciences, Professor\\nJuraev Fazliddin Orovich\",\"Doctor of technical sciences, professor\\nNuriddinov Khurram\",\"Doctor of Technical Sciences, Professor\\nOlimov Hamid Haydarovich\",\"Doctor of Philosophy in Technical Sciences Associate Professor\\nHasanov Ulug Ibragimovich\",\"Doctor of Philosophy in Technical Sciences, Associate Professor\\nJurayev Akram Azamat oglu\",\"Doctor of Philosophy in Technical Sciences, docent.\\nKochkorov Jurat Jalilovich\",\"Doctor of philosophy in technical sciences, associate professor\\nOstonov Shukhrat Saidovich\",\"Senior Lecturer\\nErgashev Zuhriddin\",\"Doctor\\nof philosophy in technical sciences Orziyev Sardor Samandarovich\",\"Doctor\\nof philosophy in technical sciences Jurayev Asliddin Nasriddin oglu\",\"Doctor\\nof Philosophy in Technical Sciences Rozikulov Jasur Uktam oglu\",\"Assistant-teacher\\nRozikulov Step Istamovich\",\"Assistant-teacher:\\nIsakov Zafarjon Shukhrat oglu\",\"Assistant-teacher\\nHalimov Tilavjon Azamat oglu\"]},{\"key\":\"prepared_specialists\",\"title\":\"\\u0627\\u0644\\u062a\\u062e\\u0635\\u0635\\u0627\\u062a \\u0627\\u0644\\u062a\\u064a \\u064a\\u062a\\u0645 \\u0625\\u0639\\u062f\\u0627\\u062f\\u0647\\u0627\",\"items\":[\"Bachelor\'s degree\\n60812400-Mechanization of water management and melioration works\\n60810100-Mechanization of agriculture\\nJudiciary\\n70811210-Mechanization of hydro-exchanization works\\n70811211 - Machines and equipment for melioration construction\\n70810100-Mechanization of agriculture\\n05.07.01 - Agricultural machinery and melioration machines. Mechanization of agricultural and land reclamation works\"]},{\"key\":\"subjects\",\"title\":\"\\u0627\\u0644\\u0645\\u0642\\u0631\\u0631\\u0627\\u062a \\u0627\\u0644\\u062f\\u0631\\u0627\\u0633\\u064a\\u0629\",\"items\":[\"Bachelor\'s Degree:\\n1. Fundamentals\\nof Agricultural Engineering 2. Technology of\\nbreeding livestock products 3. Reclamation and Construction\\nMachinery 4. Material science and technology of constructive materials\\n5. Interoperability, Standardization and Technical Measurement\\n6. Mechanization of agricultural production\\n7. Agricultural machinery\\n8. Construction machinery\\n9. Watering techniques\\n10. Tractor and Vehicles\\n11. Net Agriculture\\n12. Melioration techniques\\n13. Fuel, lubricants and technical fluids\\n14. Techniques and technologies of livestock\\n15. Integrated mechanization of irrigation and melioration\\nworks 16. Reliability of Machines and Fundamentals\\nof Repair 17. Technology of land reclamation and water management\\nworks 18. Operation of melioration and water management equipment\\n19. Use of machinery and tractor parks in agriculture\\n20. Agricultural Technology and Technical Service\\n21. Horticulture and Vegetable Machinery\\n22. Innovative techniques and technologies and their transfer\\n23. Modern techniques and technologies used in water management\\n24. Basics of\\ncattle breeding 25. Fundamentals of\\nAgricultural Engineering 26. Material handling equipment and equipment\\n27. Design of maintenance and repair facilities\\n28. Traffic rules and traffic safety\\nJudiciary\\n1. Research Work and MDT\\n2. Reclamation Sludge Equipment\\nand Equipment 3. Scientific foundations\\nof the organization of land reclamation construction 4. Engineering Logistics and Modification\\n5. Research Papers\\n6. Theoretical foundations of the design of melioration machines\\n7. Scientific and pedagogical work and scientific seminar\\n8. Basics\\nof maintenance of machines for land reclamation construction 9. Fundamentals of Technological Machine Design\\n10. Theoretical Foundations of Irrigation Machine Design\\n11. Scientific Foundations of\\nTechnical Regulation 12. Fundamentals\\nof production of resource estimate standards (ShNQ.IKN) 13. Hydroexotechnics\\n14. Technology of Drainage System\\nConstruction 15. Volumetric Hydrodynamics\\n16. Theoretical foundations of the use of construction and melioration\\nmachines 17. Technologies for the construction and use of indoor horizontal drains\\n18. Technologies and systems of land reclamation\\nconstruction 19. Fundamentals of Digital Technique and Digital Systems\\n20. Agriculture SmartAgriculture (Technologies and Techniques)\",\"Republication of publications\"]},{\"key\":\"research\",\"title\":\"\\u0627\\u0644\\u0623\\u0639\\u0645\\u0627\\u0644 \\u0627\\u0644\\u0628\\u062d\\u062b\\u064a\\u0629\",\"items\":[\"In order to improve mechanized processes of agriculture and water management, reduce energy consumption, increase service life and work efficiency, at the cage \\\"Scientific Foundations of Improving the Efficiency of Land Leveling Machines in Water Resources Saving\\\", \\\"Technical and Technological Foundations of Mechanization of Longitudinal and Transverse Flooring Processes between Goose Rows\\\", \\\"The main development of energy-efficient soils in the climatic conditions of the Bukhara valley scientific and technological foundations of the system of processing machines \\\",\\\" Substantiation of the dimensions of the equipment for irrigation of goose with liquid biofertilizers \\\", \\\"Substantiation of parameters of a device for making canvases from biohumus \\\".\"]},{\"key\":\"cooperation\",\"title\":\"\\u0627\\u0644\\u062a\\u0639\\u0627\\u0648\\u0646\",\"items\":[\"1. Kursk State Agrarian 2\\n. North Docota State University (USA)\\n3. \\\"Belarusian State Agrarian Technical University\\\"\\n4. Humboldt University of Berlin (Germany)\\n5. Obuda University (Vengriya)\\n6. South-West State University (Russia)\\n7. Iowa State University (USA)\\n8. INTI International University (Malaysia)\"]},{\"key\":\"plans\",\"title\":\"\\u0627\\u0644\\u062e\\u0637\\u0637 \\u0627\\u0644\\u0645\\u0633\\u062a\\u0642\\u0628\\u0644\\u064a\\u0629\",\"items\":[\"1. Prospective work to further improve the quality of education:\\n- improvement of the academic work at the institute by studying the experience abroad in the training of engineers;\\n- to expand the integration of education with work processes in manufacturing enterprises (DUAL education), including production practices directly with work processes in production enterprises;\\n\\u2013 widespread use of the production potential of enterprises in training personnel for production enterprises and carrying out joint scientific and technical developments;\\n\\u2013 the introduction of training, retraining and advanced training of personnel in new directions of technical and technological development, taking into account the requirements and needs of production;\\n\\u2013 regularly improve the qualifications of the department\'s teaching staff in the field of advanced technologies through the organization of internships in direct production;\\n\\u2013 attract highly qualified production personnel to the educational process and pedagogical activities, as well as organize seminars, master classes and dual classes with industry experts;\\n- Widespread use of interactive methods such as \\\"Case study\\\", \\\"Debate\\\", \\\"Brainstorming\\\" in the classroom;\\n- widespread use of information and communication technologies in organizing distance or hybrid lessons through platforms such as Moodle, Google Classroom, Zoom, MS Teams;\\n- Further development of classes - laboratories, seminars, projects that allow students to gain experience in a real environment.\\n2. Prospective work on the use of modern laboratories of enterprises in the educational process:\\nBased on the existing conditions and capabilities in the region, the registration of contracts with enterprises for a certain part of training in modern laboratories on the basis of enterprises of Bukhara cities and districts of Bukhara and the expansion of its timely implementation.\\n3. Future work on increasing the scientific potential of the department:\\n\\u2022 creating sufficient conditions for conducting scientific research work of young staff of the department.\\n\\u2022 To select students from among the graduates of the department\'s and master\'s programs with high knowledge and social culture, to improve their language proficiency and to interest them in scientific work;\\n\\u2022 Interest among gifted students, masters and teachers to develop startup ideas, innovative practical and fundamental projects and win grands.\\n4. Future work on improving the foreign relations of the department:\\n\\u2022 Find the universities of higher education in the foreign TOP 1000, having the trends and specialties of study in the department;\\n\\u2022 sign a memorandum of cooperation with higher educational institutions, establish scientific ties with professors and teachers, jointly implement foreign grants and publish scientific articles included in the SCOPUS database;\\n\\u2022 Organization of internships of the leading professors of the department in the top 1000 foreign universities and attract foreign university professors to the department and establish academic exchange.\"]}]', 'قسم التقنيات الهندسية الزراعية وإدارة المياه', 'The basis of the department \"Agricultural and water management technique technology\" was established as a higher educational institution in the education system of the Republic of Uzbekistan on August 20, 2010 under the name of the department \"Genera', '2026-07-26 00:16:43', '2026-07-27 06:31:48');
INSERT INTO `department_translations` (`id`, `department_id`, `locale`, `name`, `short_name`, `description`, `content_sections`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('37', '10', 'en', 'Department of Land Use and State Cadastre', 'Land Use and State Cadastre', 'Taking into account the growing scale of tasks of improving the land reclamation state, as well as the peculiarities of the soil and climatic conditions, mineralization and salinity of agricultural lands in certain regions, including in the Bukhara valley, and in order to train highly qualified specialists for this important area of the country\'s economy, the Cabinet of Ministers of the Republic of Uzbekistan approved the Decree of the Cabinet of Ministers of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated August 20, 2010 \"Tashkent irrigation and On the organization of the Bukhara branch of the Institute of Melioration \"The Department of Land Management and Land Cadastre\" was organized as part of the organizational structure of the faculty \"Hydromelioration\".\nThe department was organized with the name \"Land Planning and Land Cadastre\" in 2010. At present, it is called \"Land Use and State Cadastres\". Prominent scientists - professors S. Boriev and U. Tadzhiev made a great contribution to the development of the department for a long time. The department is headed by associate professor F. Hamidov, associate professor I. Islamov, and since 2022, associate professor S. Asatov. Based on their specialties, the faculty of the department \"Land Resources Use and State Cadastres\" are engaged in various problems in agriculture.\nIn recent years, the department has paid special attention to the introduction of scientific results into the academic process. The results of scientific research are widely used in the performance of lecture, laboratory and practice lessons, as well as in the preparation of course designs, training and production practice. The department is given : Cabinet of Ministers Resolution of 824 \"On the procedure for introducing the credit-modular system in the educational process in higher education institutions\" and all the law \"On Education\" adopted by the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan on higher education, It works in accordance with the decisions of the Republic of Uzbekistan.\nCurrently, the department is organized in accordance with the Decree of the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated January 24, 2025 \"Bukhara State Technical Laboratory Decree No. PQ-22 \"On the establishment of the Bukhara Engineering and Technological Institute and the Bukhara Institute of Management of Natural Resources in the Bukhara State Technical University\" has its activity.\nThe professors and teachers of the department have introduced electronic textbooks, teaching aids, lecture texts, methodological instructions, control questions and test suites for use in the \"Ziyonet\" and international Internet networks. Video lessons in all subjects are constantly posted on YouTube.\nThe department includes \"Land cadastre and land management\", \"Geodesy and geoinformatics\", \"Ecology and environmental protection\", \"Hydrology\", \"Hydrology\", \"Mechanics of water management and meliorationleveling \",\" Hydrotechnical facilities and the use of pumping stations \"and other areas of education give lectures and practical lessons. Today, due to the peculiarities of the disciplines taught in the department, lessons are used with the use of \"presentation\", \"Mental attack\", \"Discussion\", \"6x6x6\", \"Black box\" and other types of pedagogical technology.', '[{\"key\":\"overview\",\"title\":\"Overview\",\"items\":[\"Department of Land Use and State Cadastre      \\n\\nHead of the Department of land use and state cadastres\\nAsatov Sayitqul Rahimberdiyevich\\n Reception time: Dushanba-Juma (14:00-16:00 gacha)\\n Phone: +998 (91) 91 408 50 13\\n Email: -\"]},{\"key\":\"history\",\"title\":\"Department History\",\"items\":[\"Taking into account the growing scale of tasks of improving the land reclamation state, as well as the peculiarities of the soil and climatic conditions, mineralization and salinity of agricultural lands in certain regions, including in the Bukhara valley, and in order to train highly qualified specialists for this important area of the country\'s economy, the Cabinet of Ministers of the Republic of Uzbekistan approved the Decree of the Cabinet of Ministers of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated August 20, 2010 \\\"Tashkent irrigation and On the organization of the Bukhara branch of the Institute of Melioration \\\"The Department of Land Management and Land Cadastre\\\" was organized as part of the organizational structure of the faculty \\\"Hydromelioration\\\".\\nThe department was organized with the name \\\"Land Planning and Land Cadastre\\\" in 2010. At present, it is called \\\"Land Use and State Cadastres\\\". Prominent scientists - professors S. Boriev and U. Tadzhiev made a great contribution to the development of the department for a long time. The department is headed by associate professor F. Hamidov, associate professor I. Islamov, and since 2022, associate professor S. Asatov. Based on their specialties, the faculty of the department \\\"Land Resources Use and State Cadastres\\\" are engaged in various problems in agriculture.\\nIn recent years, the department has paid special attention to the introduction of scientific results into the academic process. The results of scientific research are widely used in the performance of lecture, laboratory and practice lessons, as well as in the preparation of course designs, training and production practice. The department is given : Cabinet of Ministers Resolution of 824 \\\"On the procedure for introducing the credit-modular system in the educational process in higher education institutions\\\" and all the law \\\"On Education\\\" adopted by the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan on higher education, It works in accordance with the decisions of the Republic of Uzbekistan.\\nCurrently, the department is organized in accordance with the Decree of the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated January 24, 2025 \\\"Bukhara State Technical Laboratory Decree No. PQ-22 \\\"On the establishment of the Bukhara Engineering and Technological Institute and the Bukhara Institute of Management of Natural Resources in the Bukhara State Technical University\\\" has its activity.\\nThe professors and teachers of the department have introduced electronic textbooks, teaching aids, lecture texts, methodological instructions, control questions and test suites for use in the \\\"Ziyonet\\\" and international Internet networks. Video lessons in all subjects are constantly posted on YouTube.\\nThe department includes \\\"Land cadastre and land management\\\", \\\"Geodesy and geoinformatics\\\", \\\"Ecology and environmental protection\\\", \\\"Hydrology\\\", \\\"Hydrology\\\", \\\"Mechanics of water management and meliorationleveling \\\",\\\" Hydrotechnical facilities and the use of pumping stations \\\"and other areas of education give lectures and practical lessons. Today, due to the peculiarities of the disciplines taught in the department, lessons are used with the use of \\\"presentation\\\", \\\"Mental attack\\\", \\\"Discussion\\\", \\\"6x6x6\\\", \\\"Black box\\\" and other types of pedagogical technology.\"]},{\"key\":\"staff\",\"title\":\"Professor-Teachers of the Department\",\"items\":[\"Head of the Department Doctor of Philosophy of Biological Sciences, Associate Professor\\nAsatov Sayitkul Rakhimberdiyevich\",\"Doctor of Philosophy of Technical Sciences, Professor.\\nHamidov Fayzullo Ramazonovich\",\"Doctor of Agricultural Sciences, Professor\\nIslamov Ismail\",\"Doctor of philosophy of technical sciences, professor\\nKhudoyberdiev Feruz Shamshodovich\",\"Doctor of philosophy of technical sciences, associate professor\\nSattorov Shahzod Yarashovich\",\"Doctor of Philosophy of Agricultural Sciences, associate professor\\nAdizov Shukhrat Bafoyevich\",\"Doctor of philosophy of technical sciences, associate professor\\nPirimov Jonibek Jumamurodovich\",\"Doctor of Philosophy of Biological Sciences Karimov\\nErkin Kadirovich\",\"Senior Lecturer\\nHamroyev Salahiddin Atoyevich\",\"Senior Lecturer\\nAbduloyev Ashraf Muzafarovich\",\"Senior teacher\\nAhmadov Behzod Obid oglu\",\"assistent\\nIzatov Elmir Najmidinovich\",\"assistent\\nEgamova Dilchehra Adizovna\",\"Assistant\\nNuriddinov Otabek Xurramovich\",\"assistent\\nOltinov Sobir Hayot o\'g\'li\",\"assistant\\nRajabova Gullola Islomovna\"]},{\"key\":\"prepared_specialists\",\"title\":\"Prepared Specialists\",\"items\":[\"BAKALAVRIAT\\n60811600 - Yer kadastri va yer tuzish\\n60721700 - Kadastr\\n60721500 - Geodeziya va geoinformatika\\n60721600 - Kartografiya va masofadan zondlash\\n60810300 - Tuproqlar bonitirovkasi va yer degradatsiyasi\\nMAGISTRATURA\\n70811601 \\u2013 Yer resurslaridan foydalanish va boshqarish\\n70721601 \\u2013 Yerni masofadan zondlash va GAT-texnologiyalari\",\"KAFEDRADA O\\u2018QITILADIGAN FANLAR\\nBakalavriat:\\n1. Kartografik dizayn;\\n2. Geodeziya;\\n3. Landshafshunoslik asoslari;\\n4. Kartografiya;\\n5. Davlat kadastri asoslari;\\n6. Mutaxassislikka kirish;\\n7. Oliy geodeziya;\\n8. Kartashunoslik;\\n9. Yer resurslarini boshqarish;\\n10. Zamonaviy geodezik asboblar;\\n11. Yer tuzishda geodezik ishlar;\\n12. Yer tuzishni loyihalash;\\n13. Yer tuzishning nazariy asoslari;\\n14. Hududlar kadastri ;\\n15. Raqamli kartografiya;\\n16. Ma\\u2019lumotlarni olish va integratsiyalash;\\n17. Raqamli yer kadastri;\\n18. Yer tuzishni loyihalashda avtomatlashgan tizimlar;\\n19. Yer tuzish ishlarini tashkil qilish va rejalshtirish;\\n20. Yer munosobatlarini tartibga solish;\\n21. Injenerlik geodeziyasi;\\n22. Tuproqshunoslik va o\\u2018simliklar anatomiyasi;\\n23. Tuproqshunoslik ;\\n24. Geoaxborot tizimlari asoslari;\\n25. Geoaxborot tizim va texnologiyalari;\\n26. Raqamli fotogrammeriya;\\n27. GAT da uch o`lchamli modellashtirish;\\n28. Geoma`lumotlar bazasi va arxitekturasi;\\nMagistratura\\n1. Ilmiy tadqiqot metodologiyasi\\n2. Yerdan foydalanishda integratsion boshqaruv\\n3. Hududlarni rivojlantirish\\n4. Yerdan foydalanish iqtisodi\\n5. Yer resurslarini boshqarishning huquqiy asoslari\\n6. Maxsus fanlarni o\\u2018qitish metodikasi\\n7. Yer uchastkalarini shakllantirish\\n8. Yer uchastkalarini hisobini yuritish va baholash\\n9. Ko`chmas mulkni boshqarish\",\"Darslik va o\\u2018quv qo\\u2018llanmalar\\n2024-2025 o\\u2018quv yilida Respublikada ta\\u2019lim sifatini oshirishga qaratilgan va zifalarning ijrosini ta\\u2019minlash hamda o\\u2018quv adabiyotlarining yangi avlodini yaratish konsepsiyasi talablari asosida kafedrada A.Abdulloyev, Sh.Sattorov, E.Karimov J.Primovlar tomonidan \\u201cKaratashunoslik\\u201d; A.Abdulloyev, Sh.Sattorov, S.Asatov, R.Oymatovlar tomonidan \\u201cInjenerlik geodeziyasi\\u201d; Sh.Adizov tomonidan \\u201cYer monitoringi\\u201d; S.Xamrayev tomonidan \\u201cBino-inshootlar davlat kadastri\\u201d; S.Asatov va F.Xudoyberdiyev tomonidan \\u201cYer uchastkalarini shakillantirish\\u201d o\\u2018quv qo\\u2018llanmalar va S.Xamrayev tomonidan \\u201cBino-inshootlar davlat kadastri\\u201d; F.Xudoyberdiyev tomonidan \\u201cYer uchastkalarini shakillantirish\\u201d nomli, darsliklar institut kengashidan o\\u2018tkazilib, oliy ta\\u2019lim va zirligi tomonidan guvohnomalar olindi va chop etish uchun tavsiya etildi.\"]},{\"key\":\"research\",\"title\":\"Research Work\",\"items\":[\"Currently, 25 professor-teachers serve at the newly formed department. Of them 8 professors and PhD degrees, 6 associate professors, 2 senior lecturers and 9 assistants. The scientific potential is 36%. Over the last 14 years, 10 textbooks, 15 teaching aids, more than 1000 scientific articles, 56 methodological guidelines have been published by professors and teachers of the department.\\nNowadays, professors and students of the department conduct research on the following topics: Rational organization of the use of agricultural land in the conditions of environmental unstability (on the example of the Bukhara oasis), optimization of the composition of agricultural land species in clusters, introduction of innovative technologies for monitoring agricultural lands.\"]},{\"key\":\"cooperation\",\"title\":\"Cooperation\",\"items\":[\"The department cooperates with the University of Usak in Turkey. From November 25 to December 6, 2024, a short-term internship was carried out by Khudoyberdiev F.Sh, Sattorov Sh.Y., Adizov Sh.B. and master\'s students Bobojonov S.O.\\nDuring the internship, as part of the exchange of experience between universities, lectures were organized by professors and teachers, and they got acquainted with the laboratory equipment. Electronic copies of necessary scientific literature were brought in from the Information Resource Center.\\nAn agreement was signed with the Faculty of Agriculture on the organization of online lectures on relevant subjects in Kefedra.\"]}]', 'Department of Land Use and State Cadastre', 'Taking into account the growing scale of tasks of improving the land reclamation state, as well as the peculiarities of the soil and climatic conditions, mineralization and salinity of agricultural lands in certain regions, including in the Bukhara v', '2026-07-26 00:16:43', '2026-07-27 06:31:49');
INSERT INTO `department_translations` (`id`, `department_id`, `locale`, `name`, `short_name`, `description`, `content_sections`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('38', '10', 'uz', 'Department of Land Resources Management and State Land Cadastres', 'Land Resources Management and State Land Cadastres', 'Taking into account the growing scale of tasks of improving the land reclamation state, as well as the peculiarities of the soil and climatic conditions, mineralization and salinity of agricultural lands in certain regions, including in the Bukhara valley, and in order to train highly qualified specialists for this important area of the country\'s economy, the Cabinet of Ministers of the Republic of Uzbekistan approved the Decree of the Cabinet of Ministers of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated August 20, 2010 \"Tashkent irrigation and On the organization of the Bukhara branch of the Institute of Melioration \"The Department of Land Management and Land Cadastre\" was organized as part of the organizational structure of the faculty \"Hydromelioration\".\nThe department was organized with the name \"Land Planning and Land Cadastre\" in 2010. At present, it is called \"Land Use and State Cadastres\". Prominent scientists - professors S. Boriev and U. Tadzhiev made a great contribution to the development of the department for a long time. The department is headed by associate professor F. Hamidov, associate professor I. Islamov, and since 2022, associate professor S. Asatov. Based on their specialties, the faculty of the department \"Land Resources Use and State Cadastres\" are engaged in various problems in agriculture.\nIn recent years, the department has paid special attention to the introduction of scientific results into the academic process. The results of scientific research are widely used in the performance of lecture, laboratory and practice lessons, as well as in the preparation of course designs, training and production practice. The department is given : Cabinet of Ministers Resolution of 824 \"On the procedure for introducing the credit-modular system in the educational process in higher education institutions\" and all the law \"On Education\" adopted by the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan on higher education, It works in accordance with the decisions of the Republic of Uzbekistan.\nCurrently, the department is organized in accordance with the Decree of the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated January 24, 2025 \"Bukhara State Technical Laboratory Decree No. PQ-22 \"On the establishment of the Bukhara Engineering and Technological Institute and the Bukhara Institute of Management of Natural Resources in the Bukhara State Technical University\" has its activity.\nThe professors and teachers of the department have introduced electronic textbooks, teaching aids, lecture texts, methodological instructions, control questions and test suites for use in the \"Ziyonet\" and international Internet networks. Video lessons in all subjects are constantly posted on YouTube.\nThe department includes \"Land cadastre and land management\", \"Geodesy and geoinformatics\", \"Ecology and environmental protection\", \"Hydrology\", \"Hydrology\", \"Mechanics of water management and meliorationleveling \",\" Hydrotechnical facilities and the use of pumping stations \"and other areas of education give lectures and practical lessons. Today, due to the peculiarities of the disciplines taught in the department, lessons are used with the use of \"presentation\", \"Mental attack\", \"Discussion\", \"6x6x6\", \"Black box\" and other types of pedagogical technology.', '[{\"key\":\"overview\",\"title\":\"Umumiy ma\\u02bclumot\",\"items\":[\"Department of Land Use and State Cadastre      \\n\\nHead of the Department of land use and state cadastres\\nAsatov Sayitqul Rahimberdiyevich\\n Reception time: Dushanba-Juma (14:00-16:00 gacha)\\n Phone: +998 (91) 91 408 50 13\\n Email: -\"]},{\"key\":\"history\",\"title\":\"Kafedra tarixi\",\"items\":[\"Taking into account the growing scale of tasks of improving the land reclamation state, as well as the peculiarities of the soil and climatic conditions, mineralization and salinity of agricultural lands in certain regions, including in the Bukhara valley, and in order to train highly qualified specialists for this important area of the country\'s economy, the Cabinet of Ministers of the Republic of Uzbekistan approved the Decree of the Cabinet of Ministers of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated August 20, 2010 \\\"Tashkent irrigation and On the organization of the Bukhara branch of the Institute of Melioration \\\"The Department of Land Management and Land Cadastre\\\" was organized as part of the organizational structure of the faculty \\\"Hydromelioration\\\".\\nThe department was organized with the name \\\"Land Planning and Land Cadastre\\\" in 2010. At present, it is called \\\"Land Use and State Cadastres\\\". Prominent scientists - professors S. Boriev and U. Tadzhiev made a great contribution to the development of the department for a long time. The department is headed by associate professor F. Hamidov, associate professor I. Islamov, and since 2022, associate professor S. Asatov. Based on their specialties, the faculty of the department \\\"Land Resources Use and State Cadastres\\\" are engaged in various problems in agriculture.\\nIn recent years, the department has paid special attention to the introduction of scientific results into the academic process. The results of scientific research are widely used in the performance of lecture, laboratory and practice lessons, as well as in the preparation of course designs, training and production practice. The department is given : Cabinet of Ministers Resolution of 824 \\\"On the procedure for introducing the credit-modular system in the educational process in higher education institutions\\\" and all the law \\\"On Education\\\" adopted by the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan on higher education, It works in accordance with the decisions of the Republic of Uzbekistan.\\nCurrently, the department is organized in accordance with the Decree of the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated January 24, 2025 \\\"Bukhara State Technical Laboratory Decree No. PQ-22 \\\"On the establishment of the Bukhara Engineering and Technological Institute and the Bukhara Institute of Management of Natural Resources in the Bukhara State Technical University\\\" has its activity.\\nThe professors and teachers of the department have introduced electronic textbooks, teaching aids, lecture texts, methodological instructions, control questions and test suites for use in the \\\"Ziyonet\\\" and international Internet networks. Video lessons in all subjects are constantly posted on YouTube.\\nThe department includes \\\"Land cadastre and land management\\\", \\\"Geodesy and geoinformatics\\\", \\\"Ecology and environmental protection\\\", \\\"Hydrology\\\", \\\"Hydrology\\\", \\\"Mechanics of water management and meliorationleveling \\\",\\\" Hydrotechnical facilities and the use of pumping stations \\\"and other areas of education give lectures and practical lessons. Today, due to the peculiarities of the disciplines taught in the department, lessons are used with the use of \\\"presentation\\\", \\\"Mental attack\\\", \\\"Discussion\\\", \\\"6x6x6\\\", \\\"Black box\\\" and other types of pedagogical technology.\"]},{\"key\":\"staff\",\"title\":\"Kafedra professor-o\\u2018qituvchilari\",\"items\":[\"Head of the Department Doctor of Philosophy of Biological Sciences, Associate Professor\\nAsatov Sayitkul Rakhimberdiyevich\",\"Doctor of Philosophy of Technical Sciences, Professor.\\nHamidov Fayzullo Ramazonovich\",\"Doctor of Agricultural Sciences, Professor\\nIslamov Ismail\",\"Doctor of philosophy of technical sciences, professor\\nKhudoyberdiev Feruz Shamshodovich\",\"Doctor of philosophy of technical sciences, associate professor\\nSattorov Shahzod Yarashovich\",\"Doctor of Philosophy of Agricultural Sciences, associate professor\\nAdizov Shukhrat Bafoyevich\",\"Doctor of philosophy of technical sciences, associate professor\\nPirimov Jonibek Jumamurodovich\",\"Doctor of Philosophy of Biological Sciences Karimov\\nErkin Kadirovich\",\"Senior Lecturer\\nHamroyev Salahiddin Atoyevich\",\"Senior Lecturer\\nAbduloyev Ashraf Muzafarovich\",\"Senior teacher\\nAhmadov Behzod Obid oglu\",\"assistent\\nIzatov Elmir Najmidinovich\",\"assistent\\nEgamova Dilchehra Adizovna\",\"Assistant\\nNuriddinov Otabek Xurramovich\",\"assistent\\nOltinov Sobir Hayot o\'g\'li\",\"assistant\\nRajabova Gullola Islomovna\"]},{\"key\":\"prepared_specialists\",\"title\":\"Tayyorlanadigan mutaxassislar\",\"items\":[\"BAKALAVRIAT\\n60811600 - Yer kadastri va yer tuzish\\n60721700 - Kadastr\\n60721500 - Geodeziya va geoinformatika\\n60721600 - Kartografiya va masofadan zondlash\\n60810300 - Tuproqlar bonitirovkasi va yer degradatsiyasi\\nMAGISTRATURA\\n70811601 \\u2013 Yer resurslaridan foydalanish va boshqarish\\n70721601 \\u2013 Yerni masofadan zondlash va GAT-texnologiyalari\",\"KAFEDRADA O\\u2018QITILADIGAN FANLAR\\nBakalavriat:\\n1. Kartografik dizayn;\\n2. Geodeziya;\\n3. Landshafshunoslik asoslari;\\n4. Kartografiya;\\n5. Davlat kadastri asoslari;\\n6. Mutaxassislikka kirish;\\n7. Oliy geodeziya;\\n8. Kartashunoslik;\\n9. Yer resurslarini boshqarish;\\n10. Zamonaviy geodezik asboblar;\\n11. Yer tuzishda geodezik ishlar;\\n12. Yer tuzishni loyihalash;\\n13. Yer tuzishning nazariy asoslari;\\n14. Hududlar kadastri ;\\n15. Raqamli kartografiya;\\n16. Ma\\u2019lumotlarni olish va integratsiyalash;\\n17. Raqamli yer kadastri;\\n18. Yer tuzishni loyihalashda avtomatlashgan tizimlar;\\n19. Yer tuzish ishlarini tashkil qilish va rejalshtirish;\\n20. Yer munosobatlarini tartibga solish;\\n21. Injenerlik geodeziyasi;\\n22. Tuproqshunoslik va o\\u2018simliklar anatomiyasi;\\n23. Tuproqshunoslik ;\\n24. Geoaxborot tizimlari asoslari;\\n25. Geoaxborot tizim va texnologiyalari;\\n26. Raqamli fotogrammeriya;\\n27. GAT da uch o`lchamli modellashtirish;\\n28. Geoma`lumotlar bazasi va arxitekturasi;\\nMagistratura\\n1. Ilmiy tadqiqot metodologiyasi\\n2. Yerdan foydalanishda integratsion boshqaruv\\n3. Hududlarni rivojlantirish\\n4. Yerdan foydalanish iqtisodi\\n5. Yer resurslarini boshqarishning huquqiy asoslari\\n6. Maxsus fanlarni o\\u2018qitish metodikasi\\n7. Yer uchastkalarini shakllantirish\\n8. Yer uchastkalarini hisobini yuritish va baholash\\n9. Ko`chmas mulkni boshqarish\",\"Darslik va o\\u2018quv qo\\u2018llanmalar\\n2024-2025 o\\u2018quv yilida Respublikada ta\\u2019lim sifatini oshirishga qaratilgan va zifalarning ijrosini ta\\u2019minlash hamda o\\u2018quv adabiyotlarining yangi avlodini yaratish konsepsiyasi talablari asosida kafedrada A.Abdulloyev, Sh.Sattorov, E.Karimov J.Primovlar tomonidan \\u201cKaratashunoslik\\u201d; A.Abdulloyev, Sh.Sattorov, S.Asatov, R.Oymatovlar tomonidan \\u201cInjenerlik geodeziyasi\\u201d; Sh.Adizov tomonidan \\u201cYer monitoringi\\u201d; S.Xamrayev tomonidan \\u201cBino-inshootlar davlat kadastri\\u201d; S.Asatov va F.Xudoyberdiyev tomonidan \\u201cYer uchastkalarini shakillantirish\\u201d o\\u2018quv qo\\u2018llanmalar va S.Xamrayev tomonidan \\u201cBino-inshootlar davlat kadastri\\u201d; F.Xudoyberdiyev tomonidan \\u201cYer uchastkalarini shakillantirish\\u201d nomli, darsliklar institut kengashidan o\\u2018tkazilib, oliy ta\\u2019lim va zirligi tomonidan guvohnomalar olindi va chop etish uchun tavsiya etildi.\"]},{\"key\":\"research\",\"title\":\"Ilmiy-tadqiqot ishlari\",\"items\":[\"Currently, 25 professor-teachers serve at the newly formed department. Of them 8 professors and PhD degrees, 6 associate professors, 2 senior lecturers and 9 assistants. The scientific potential is 36%. Over the last 14 years, 10 textbooks, 15 teaching aids, more than 1000 scientific articles, 56 methodological guidelines have been published by professors and teachers of the department.\\nNowadays, professors and students of the department conduct research on the following topics: Rational organization of the use of agricultural land in the conditions of environmental unstability (on the example of the Bukhara oasis), optimization of the composition of agricultural land species in clusters, introduction of innovative technologies for monitoring agricultural lands.\"]},{\"key\":\"cooperation\",\"title\":\"Hamkorlik\",\"items\":[\"The department cooperates with the University of Usak in Turkey. From November 25 to December 6, 2024, a short-term internship was carried out by Khudoyberdiev F.Sh, Sattorov Sh.Y., Adizov Sh.B. and master\'s students Bobojonov S.O.\\nDuring the internship, as part of the exchange of experience between universities, lectures were organized by professors and teachers, and they got acquainted with the laboratory equipment. Electronic copies of necessary scientific literature were brought in from the Information Resource Center.\\nAn agreement was signed with the Faculty of Agriculture on the organization of online lectures on relevant subjects in Kefedra.\"]}]', 'Department of Land Resources Management and State Land Cadastres', 'Taking into account the growing scale of tasks of improving the land reclamation state, as well as the peculiarities of the soil and climatic conditions, mineralization and salinity of agricultural lands in certain regions, including in the Bukhara v', '2026-07-26 00:16:43', '2026-07-27 06:31:49');
INSERT INTO `department_translations` (`id`, `department_id`, `locale`, `name`, `short_name`, `description`, `content_sections`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('39', '10', 'ru', 'Кафедра использования земельных ресурсов и государственного кадастра', 'Кафедра использования земельных ресурсов и государственного кадастра', 'Taking into account the growing scale of tasks of improving the land reclamation state, as well as the peculiarities of the soil and climatic conditions, mineralization and salinity of agricultural lands in certain regions, including in the Bukhara valley, and in order to train highly qualified specialists for this important area of the country\'s economy, the Cabinet of Ministers of the Republic of Uzbekistan approved the Decree of the Cabinet of Ministers of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated August 20, 2010 \"Tashkent irrigation and On the organization of the Bukhara branch of the Institute of Melioration \"The Department of Land Management and Land Cadastre\" was organized as part of the organizational structure of the faculty \"Hydromelioration\".\nThe department was organized with the name \"Land Planning and Land Cadastre\" in 2010. At present, it is called \"Land Use and State Cadastres\". Prominent scientists - professors S. Boriev and U. Tadzhiev made a great contribution to the development of the department for a long time. The department is headed by associate professor F. Hamidov, associate professor I. Islamov, and since 2022, associate professor S. Asatov. Based on their specialties, the faculty of the department \"Land Resources Use and State Cadastres\" are engaged in various problems in agriculture.\nIn recent years, the department has paid special attention to the introduction of scientific results into the academic process. The results of scientific research are widely used in the performance of lecture, laboratory and practice lessons, as well as in the preparation of course designs, training and production practice. The department is given : Cabinet of Ministers Resolution of 824 \"On the procedure for introducing the credit-modular system in the educational process in higher education institutions\" and all the law \"On Education\" adopted by the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan on higher education, It works in accordance with the decisions of the Republic of Uzbekistan.\nCurrently, the department is organized in accordance with the Decree of the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated January 24, 2025 \"Bukhara State Technical Laboratory Decree No. PQ-22 \"On the establishment of the Bukhara Engineering and Technological Institute and the Bukhara Institute of Management of Natural Resources in the Bukhara State Technical University\" has its activity.\nThe professors and teachers of the department have introduced electronic textbooks, teaching aids, lecture texts, methodological instructions, control questions and test suites for use in the \"Ziyonet\" and international Internet networks. Video lessons in all subjects are constantly posted on YouTube.\nThe department includes \"Land cadastre and land management\", \"Geodesy and geoinformatics\", \"Ecology and environmental protection\", \"Hydrology\", \"Hydrology\", \"Mechanics of water management and meliorationleveling \",\" Hydrotechnical facilities and the use of pumping stations \"and other areas of education give lectures and practical lessons. Today, due to the peculiarities of the disciplines taught in the department, lessons are used with the use of \"presentation\", \"Mental attack\", \"Discussion\", \"6x6x6\", \"Black box\" and other types of pedagogical technology.', '[{\"key\":\"overview\",\"title\":\"\\u041e\\u0431\\u0437\\u043e\\u0440\",\"items\":[\"Department of Land Use and State Cadastre      \\n\\nHead of the Department of land use and state cadastres\\nAsatov Sayitqul Rahimberdiyevich\\n Reception time: Dushanba-Juma (14:00-16:00 gacha)\\n Phone: +998 (91) 91 408 50 1